## std/tally.pengu
## Algoritmos sobre listas: reducciones, búsqueda, estadística, ordenación,
## selección, filtrado y transformación, con una API **genérica** (`T: Num`,
## `T: Ordo`, `T: Par`, `T: Integrum`) y compatibilidad 100% con la API
## concreta de `list of int` de 0.14.x/0.15.0.
##
## Cada operación existe dos veces, como método (`calling xs.sum`) y como
## función de módulo (`calling tally.sum with xs`). Las funciones de módulo
## de la sección de compatibilidad son concretas (`list of int`), con la firma
## exacta de siempre, y delegan en los métodos; los métodos genéricos viven en
## bloques `enchanting` con su propio bound.
##
## ## Cuándo usar `tally` y cuándo `loom`
## `tally` es la familia de reducciones con **identidad natural**: una lista
## vacía colapsa a un centinela (`sum` -> 0, `product_num` -> 1, `max_val` -> 0,
## `mode` -> 0) y las estadísticas fraccionarias se truncan a `int`
## (`calling xs.mean` sobre `[1, 2]` da 1). Es lo que quieres cuando el centinela
## significa algo y no quieres ramificar.
##
## `std.loom` es la familia segura: `loom.mean` devuelve `float` (`1.5`) y
## `loom.median`/`loom.mode`/`loom.min_max` devuelven `maybe` cuando la lista
## está vacía. Los 15 nombres compartidos **no tienen la misma firma**: no son
## duplicados, son dos contratos distintos. Usa `loom` cuando una lista vacía no
## tenga respuesta y devolver un centinela ocultaría un bug.
## Ver `LANGUAGE.md` §19.1.1 y `docs/DEPRECATIONS.md`.
##
## ## Ownership
## Ninguna operación muta ni libera la lista de entrada: solo se lee
## (`essence of self`) y se devuelve un valor escalar o una **lista nueva**
## auto-banishable. Las listas de entrada pertenecen al llamador.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## import std.tally
##
## weave main into int:
##     var xs as list of int is [3, 1, 2]
##     var total as int is calling xs.sum
##     var biggest as int is calling tally.max_val with xs
##     var evens as list of int is calling xs.filter_even
##     var floats as list of float is [1.5, 0.5]
##     var fsum as float is calling floats.sum
##     return 0
## ```
##
## ## Notas de diseño
## - **Genéricos en métodos, no en funciones de módulo.** Un método no admite
##   `where`: los bounds viven en bloques `enchanting list of shard T where T:
##   Num/Ordo/Par/Integrum`. Las funciones de módulo de compatibilidad son
##   concretas (`l as list of int`), conservan la firma exacta y delegan en el
##   método; generalizar su nombre rompería `calling xs.nombre`.
## - **Sin llamadas entre genéricos.** Un cuerpo genérico no puede invocar a
##   otro `weave`/método genérico (el compilador emite la plantilla `_T`), así
##   que cada método genérico es autocontenido y los alias (`argmin`,
##   `average`, `dedup`, `filter_range`) repiten el cuerpo base.
## - **Construcción de listas genéricas.** En un cuerpo genérico `push`/`pop`
##   sobre `list of T` no son fiables: las listas nuevas salen de
##   comprehensions, y el trabajo por índices usa una lista local de índices
##   (`list of int`, `push` concreto) recorrida con otra comprehension.
## - **`at_or` y `clamp_all`** necesitan defaults de tipo `int` (un parámetro
##   genérico no admite default dependiente de `T`), así que viven en el bloque
##   concreto `list of int`.
## - **Sin tuplas.** `min_max`, `enumerate_pairs` y `partition_by` devuelven
##   `list of int`/`list of list of int` para no depender de `std.oracle`.
## - **Sin `@deprecated` real.** Los alias son `weave` normales cuyo docstring
##   empieza por `## @deprecated Use X instead.`
## - **Tests internos.** El harness `_expect*` usa `spark.panic`:
##   `import std.ward` produciría un ciclo (`ward -> tally`, E0004).
##
## ## Migración
## | Antes (0.14.x) | Ahora (0.15.0) |
## |---|---|
## | `calling tally.sum with xs` | igual, o `calling xs.sum` |
## | `calling tally.sort_asc with xs` | igual, o `calling xs.sort_asc` |
## | `calling tally.clamp_all with xs, 0, 9` | igual, o `calling xs.clamp_all with 0, 9` |
## | `calling tally.map_increment with xs, 2` | igual, o `calling xs.map_increment with 2` |
## | (nuevo) | `zip_with`, `chunk`, `windowed`, `running_sum`, `scan_left` |
## | (nuevo) | `partition_by`, `enumerate_pairs`, `min_max` |
## | (nuevo) | `frequencies`, `group_count` |

# --- Imports ------------------------------------------------------------
import std.spark

# --- Constantes públicas ------------------------------------------------

## Versión del módulo tally.
const TALLY_VERSION as string is "0.16.0"

# --- Enchantings --------------------------------------------------------

## Métodos genéricos que solo requieren valor por defecto (`donum T`):
## acceso, inversión, aplanado y selección por rango.
enchanting list of shard T where T: Donum:
    ## Primer elemento de `self`, o `donum T` si está vacía.
    weave first into T:
        if (calling self.len) == 0:
            return donum T
        self at 0

    ## Último elemento de `self`, o `donum T` si está vacía.
    weave last into T:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return donum T
        self at (n - 1)

    ## Elemento en `idx`, o `maybe none` si está fuera de rango.
    weave at_safe with idx as int into maybe T:
        if idx < 0:
            return maybe none
        if idx >= (calling self.len):
            return maybe none
        some (self at idx)

    ## Copia con los elementos en orden inverso.
    weave reverse into list of T:
        var out as list of T is for x in essence of self then x
        var n as int is calling out.len
        var i as int is 0
        while i < (n / 2):
            var tmp as T is out at i
            set out at i is (out at (n - 1 - i))
            set out at (n - 1 - i) is tmp
            set i is i + 1
        out

    ## Copia identidad; aplana un nivel de anidamiento lógico.
    weave flatten into list of T:
        for x in essence of self then x

    ## Primeros `n` elementos (recorta si `n` excede la longitud).
    weave take with n as int is 1 into list of T:
        var total as int is calling self.len
        var limit as int is n
        if limit > total:
            set limit is total
        if limit < 0:
            set limit is 0
        var idxs as list of int is list of int
        var i as int is 0
        while i < limit:
            calling idxs.push with i
            set i is i + 1
        for j in idxs then (self at j)

    ## Elementos a partir del índice `n`.
    weave drop with n as int is 1 into list of T:
        var total as int is calling self.len
        var start as int is n
        if start < 0:
            set start is 0
        var idxs as list of int is list of int
        var i as int is start
        while i < total:
            calling idxs.push with i
            set i is i + 1
        for j in idxs then (self at j)

    ## Sub-lista `[start, end_idx)`.
    weave slice_list with start as int, end_idx as int into list of T:
        var total as int is calling self.len
        var s as int is start
        if s < 0:
            set s is 0
        var e as int is end_idx
        if e > total:
            set e is total
        var idxs as list of int is list of int
        var i as int is s
        while i < e:
            calling idxs.push with i
            set i is i + 1
        for j in idxs then (self at j)

## Métodos numéricos genéricos (`+ - * /` y literales).
enchanting list of shard T where T: Num:
    ## Suma de todos los elementos; la lista vacía devuelve `donum T`.
    weave sum into T:
        var acc as T is donum T
        for x in essence of self:
            set acc is acc + x
        acc

    ## Producto de todos los elementos; la lista vacía devuelve 1.
    weave product into T:
        var acc as T is 1
        for x in essence of self:
            set acc is acc * x
        acc

    ## Media aritmética truncada hacia cero; vacía devuelve `donum T`.
    weave mean into T:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return donum T
        var acc as T is donum T
        for x in essence of self:
            set acc is acc + x
        acc / n

    ## @deprecated Use `mean` instead.
    ##
    ## Alias de `mean`.
    weave average into T:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return donum T
        var acc as T is donum T
        for x in essence of self:
            set acc is acc + x
        acc / n

    ## Suma de los cuadrados de todos los elementos.
    weave sum_of_squares into T:
        var acc as T is donum T
        for x in essence of self:
            set acc is acc + (x * x)
        acc

    ## Copia con cada elemento multiplicado por 2.
    weave map_double into list of T:
        for x in essence of self then (x * 2)

    ## Copia con cada elemento elevado al cuadrado.
    weave map_square into list of T:
        for x in essence of self then (x * x)

    ## Copia con cada elemento negado.
    weave map_negate into list of T:
        for x in essence of self then (0 - x)

    ## Copia con el escalar `k` sumado a cada elemento.
    weave map_add_scalar with k as T into list of T:
        for x in essence of self then (x + k)

    ## Copia con `delta` sumado a cada elemento (equivale a `map_add_scalar`).
    weave map_increment with delta as int is 1 into list of T:
        var d as T is delta
        for x in essence of self then (x + d)

## Métodos de orden (`< <= > >=`); `max_val`/`min_val` usan `donum T`.
enchanting list of shard T where T: Ordo:
    ## Mayor elemento; la lista vacía devuelve `donum T`.
    weave max_val into T:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return donum T
        var m as T is self at 0
        for x in essence of self:
            if x > m:
                set m is x
        m

    ## Menor elemento; la lista vacía devuelve `donum T`.
    weave min_val into T:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return donum T
        var m as T is self at 0
        for x in essence of self:
            if x < m:
                set m is x
        m

    ## Índice del primer máximo, o -1 si está vacía.
    weave max_index into int:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return -1
        var best_idx as int is 0
        var best_val as T is self at 0
        var idx as int is 0
        for x in essence of self:
            if x > best_val:
                set best_val is x
                set best_idx is idx
            set idx is idx + 1
        best_idx

    ## Índice del primer mínimo, o -1 si está vacía.
    weave min_index into int:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return -1
        var best_idx as int is 0
        var best_val as T is self at 0
        var idx as int is 0
        for x in essence of self:
            if x < best_val:
                set best_val is x
                set best_idx is idx
            set idx is idx + 1
        best_idx

    ## @deprecated Use `min_index` instead.
    ##
    ## Alias de `min_index`.
    weave argmin into int:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return -1
        var best_idx as int is 0
        var best_val as T is self at 0
        var idx as int is 0
        for x in essence of self:
            if x < best_val:
                set best_val is x
                set best_idx is idx
            set idx is idx + 1
        best_idx

    ## @deprecated Use `max_index` instead.
    ##
    ## Alias de `max_index`.
    weave argmax into int:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return -1
        var best_idx as int is 0
        var best_val as T is self at 0
        var idx as int is 0
        for x in essence of self:
            if x > best_val:
                set best_val is x
                set best_idx is idx
            set idx is idx + 1
        best_idx

    ## Copia ordenada de forma ascendente (inserción, O(n^2)).
    weave sort_asc into list of T:
        var out as list of T is for x in essence of self then x
        var n as int is calling out.len
        var i as int is 0
        while i < n:
            var j as int is i + 1
            while j < n:
                if (out at j) < (out at i):
                    var tmp as T is out at i
                    set out at i is (out at j)
                    set out at j is tmp
                set j is j + 1
            set i is i + 1
        out

    ## Copia ordenada de forma descendente (inserción, O(n^2)).
    weave sort_desc into list of T:
        var out as list of T is for x in essence of self then x
        var n as int is calling out.len
        var i as int is 0
        while i < n:
            var j as int is i + 1
            while j < n:
                if (out at j) > (out at i):
                    var tmp as T is out at i
                    set out at i is (out at j)
                    set out at j is tmp
                set j is j + 1
            set i is i + 1
        out

    ## True si `self` está ordenada de forma no descendente.
    weave is_sorted_asc into bool:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n <= 1:
            return true
        var i as int is 0
        while i < (n - 1):
            if (self at i) > (self at (i + 1)):
                return false
            set i is i + 1
        true

    ## True si `self` está ordenada de forma no ascendente.
    weave is_sorted_desc into bool:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n <= 1:
            return true
        var i as int is 0
        while i < (n - 1):
            if (self at i) < (self at (i + 1)):
                return false
            set i is i + 1
        true

    ## True si todos los elementos son estrictamente positivos.
    weave all_positive into bool:
        var zero as T is donum T
        for x in essence of self:
            if x <= zero:
                return false
        true

    ## True si al menos un elemento es estrictamente negativo.
    weave any_negative into bool:
        var zero as T is donum T
        for x in essence of self:
            if x < zero:
                return true
        false

    ## Copia con los elementos estrictamente positivos.
    weave filter_positive into list of T:
        var zero as T is donum T
        for x in essence of self when x > zero then x

    ## Copia con los elementos estrictamente negativos.
    weave filter_negative into list of T:
        var zero as T is donum T
        for x in essence of self when x < zero then x

    ## Primer elemento estrictamente mayor que `threshold`.
    weave find_first_gt with threshold as T into maybe T:
        for x in essence of self:
            if x > threshold:
                return some x
        return maybe none

    ## Primer elemento estrictamente menor que `threshold`.
    weave find_first_lt with threshold as T into maybe T:
        for x in essence of self:
            if x < threshold:
                return some x
        return maybe none

## Métodos que combinan aritmética y orden (valor absoluto, mediana, rangos).
enchanting list of shard T where T: Num, T: Ordo:
    ## Copia con el valor absoluto de cada elemento.
    weave abs_all into list of T:
        var zero as T is donum T
        for x in essence of self then (if x < zero then (zero - x) else x)

    ## Mediana tras ordenar; vacía devuelve `donum T`. Con longitud par
    ## promedia los dos valores centrales (división entera hacia cero).
    weave median into T:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return donum T
        var s as list of T is for x in essence of self then x
        var i as int is 0
        while i < n:
            var j as int is i + 1
            while j < n:
                if (s at j) < (s at i):
                    var tmp as T is s at i
                    set s at i is (s at j)
                    set s at j is tmp
                set j is j + 1
            set i is i + 1
        var mid as int is n / 2
        if (n % 2) == 1:
            return s at mid
        ((s at (mid - 1)) + (s at mid)) / 2

    ## True si todos los elementos caen en `[lo, hi]`.
    weave all_in_range with lo as T, hi as T into bool:
        for x in essence of self:
            if x < lo:
                return false
            if x > hi:
                return false
        true

    ## Copia con los elementos que caen en `[lo, hi]`.
    weave filter_in_range with lo as T, hi as T into list of T:
        for x in essence of self when x >= lo and x <= hi then x

    ## @deprecated Use `filter_in_range` instead.
    ##
    ## Alias de `filter_in_range`.
    weave filter_range with lo as T, hi as T into list of T:
        for x in essence of self when x >= lo and x <= hi then x

## Métodos que solo comparan por igualdad (`== !=`).
enchanting list of shard T where T: Par:
    ## True si todos los elementos son iguales a `donum T`.
    weave all_zero into bool:
        var zero as T is donum T
        for x in essence of self:
            if x != zero:
                return false
        true

    ## Valor más frecuente; vacía devuelve `donum T` (empates: el primero).
    weave mode into T:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if n == 0:
            return donum T
        var best as T is self at 0
        var best_count as int is 0
        for x in essence of self:
            var count_n as int is 0
            for y in essence of self:
                if y == x:
                    set count_n is count_n + 1
            if count_n > best_count:
                set best_count is count_n
                set best is x
        best

    ## Copia sin duplicados, conservando el orden de primera aparición.
    weave unique into list of T:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        var keep as list of int is list of int
        var i as int is 0
        while i < n:
            var dup as bool is false
            var j as int is 0
            while j < i:
                if (self at j) == (self at i):
                    set dup is true
                set j is j + 1
            if not dup:
                calling keep.push with i
            set i is i + 1
        for k in keep then (self at k)

    ## @deprecated Use `unique` instead.
    ##
    ## Alias de `unique`.
    weave dedup into list of T:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        var keep as list of int is list of int
        var i as int is 0
        while i < n:
            var dup as bool is false
            var j as int is 0
            while j < i:
                if (self at j) == (self at i):
                    set dup is true
                set j is j + 1
            if not dup:
                calling keep.push with i
            set i is i + 1
        for k in keep then (self at k)

    ## Número de apariciones de `item`.
    weave count_of with item as T into int:
        var count_n as int is 0
        for x in essence of self:
            if x == item:
                set count_n is count_n + 1
        count_n

    ## Índice de la última aparición de `item`, o -1 si no está.
    weave last_index_of with item as T into int:
        var i as int is (calling self.len) - 1
        while i >= 0:
            if (self at i) == item:
                return i
            set i is i - 1
        -1

## Métodos que requieren aritmética entera (`%`).
enchanting list of shard T where T: Integrum and T: Par:
    ## Copia con los elementos pares.
    weave filter_even into list of T:
        for x in essence of self when (x % 2) == 0 then x

    ## Copia con los elementos impares.
    weave filter_odd into list of T:
        for x in essence of self when (x % 2) != 0 then x

## Especializaciones concretas cuyo default depende del tipo `int`.
enchanting list of int:
    ## Elemento en `idx`, o `default` si está fuera de rango.
    weave at_or with idx as int, default as int is 0 into int:
        var n as int is calling self.len
        if idx < 0:
            return default
        if idx >= n:
            return default
        self at idx

    ## Copia con todos los valores limitados a `[lo, hi]`.
    weave clamp_all with lo as int is 0, hi as int is 100 into list of int:
        for x in essence of self then (if x < lo then lo else (if x > hi then hi else x))

# --- Funciones de módulo (compatibilidad `list of int`) -----------------

## True cuando `l` no tiene elementos.
weave is_empty with l as list of int into bool:
    return (calling l.len) == 0

## Suma aritmética de todos los elementos; la lista vacía suma 0.
weave sum with l as list of int into int:
    return calling l.sum

## Mayor elemento; la lista vacía devuelve 0.
weave max_val with l as list of int into int:
    return calling l.max_val

## Menor elemento; la lista vacía devuelve 0.
weave min_val with l as list of int into int:
    return calling l.min_val

## Concatenación de `a` y `b` en una lista nueva.
##
## ## Ownership
## Devuelve una lista nueva auto-banishable; no muta `a` ni `b`.
weave concat with a as list of int, b as list of int into list of int:
    var result as list of int is list of int
    for x in a:
        calling result.push with x
    for x in b:
        calling result.push with x
    return result

## Suma elemento a elemento hasta la lista más corta.
weave zip_sum with a as list of int, b as list of int into list of int:
    var result as list of int is list of int
    var na as int is calling a.len
    var nb as int is calling b.len
    var limit as int is na
    if nb < limit:
        set limit is nb
    var i as int is 0
    while i < limit:
        calling result.push with ((a at i) + (b at i))
        set i is i + 1
    return result

## Producto escalar de dos vectores enteros.
weave dot with a as list of int, b as list of int into int:
    var total as int is 0
    var na as int is calling a.len
    var nb as int is calling b.len
    var limit as int is na
    if nb < limit:
        set limit is nb
    var i as int is 0
    while i < limit:
        set total is total + ((a at i) * (b at i))
        set i is i + 1
    return total

## Lista nueva con `val` repetido `times` veces (`times <= 0` da lista vacía).
weave repeat with val as int, times as int into list of int:
    var result as list of int is list of int
    var i as int is 0
    while i < times:
        calling result.push with val
        set i is i + 1
    return result

## Número de elementos de `l`. Alias del built-in `l.len`.
weave len with l as list of int into int:
    return calling l.len

## Primer elemento de `l`, o 0 si está vacía.
weave first with l as list of int into int:
    return calling l.first

## Último elemento de `l`, o 0 si está vacía.
weave last with l as list of int into int:
    return calling l.last

## Elemento en `idx`, o `default` si está fuera de rango.
weave at_or with l as list of int, idx as int, default as int is 0 into int:
    return calling l.at_or with idx, default

## `some v` si `idx` está en rango, `maybe none` si no.
weave at_safe with l as list of int, idx as int into maybe int:
    return calling l.at_safe with idx

## True si `item` está en `l`. Alias del built-in `l.contains`.
weave contains with l as list of int, item as int into bool:
    return calling l.contains with item

## Índice de la primera aparición de `item`, o -1 si no está.
weave index_of with l as list of int, item as int into int:
    return calling l.index_of with item

## Índice de la última aparición de `item`, o -1 si no está.
weave last_index_of with l as list of int, item as int into int:
    return calling l.last_index_of with item

## Número de apariciones de `item` en `l`.
weave count_of with l as list of int, item as int into int:
    return calling l.count_of with item

## Primer elemento estrictamente mayor que `threshold`.
weave find_first_gt with l as list of int, threshold as int into maybe int:
    return calling l.find_first_gt with threshold

## Primer elemento estrictamente menor que `threshold`.
weave find_first_lt with l as list of int, threshold as int into maybe int:
    return calling l.find_first_lt with threshold

## Producto de todos los elementos; la lista vacía devuelve 1.
weave product with l as list of int into int:
    return calling l.product

## Índice del primer máximo, o -1 si está vacía.
weave max_index with l as list of int into int:
    return calling l.max_index

